        <span class="section-label">KIDS CLASS</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Physical-Fitness Karate</h1>
      </div>

      <p class="detail-page__lead">
        For preschoolers through junior high students in their growth years, Seishinkai karate — a full-body exercise that engages everything from the tips of the toes to the head — is ideal.<br />
        Sports centered on competition build the body through competing with others, but from a competitive standpoint they often place strain on specific parts of the body rather than offering complete full-body conditioning.<br />
        Especially during the growth years from preschool through the early elementary grades, Seishinkai's physical-fitness karate — which isn't centered on competition (sport) — is the best fit.<br />
        Seishinkai karate strengthens the core and improves physical function without placing excessive strain on any one part of the body.
      </p>

      <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair--reverse">
        <div class="detail-media--big">
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/assets/images/legacy/base/tai1.jpg"
              alt="Children training their core through karate practice"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            Children don't have the same concentration span as adults, but once they start having fun with karate, they come to love it.<br />
            Once they love it, concentration and perseverance follow naturally.<br />
            Beyond simply improving physical function, training alongside a wide range of age groups lets them experience group activity from an early age.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair">
        <div class="detail-media--big">
